  "problem": "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-(x+2)(x-1) <  0.$      \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/c764652658e603142d22e4a9ec02c59c2143bd4d5df2a38d6d6e7dd629ccf88b.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x+2)(x-1) <   0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny = -(x+2)(x-1)\n$$\n\n   \n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/cb3adba60c427e4f68bf756301a9b101ce17ca32adb8ea6ba9f3b492cccce2cc.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<    -2$ or    $x >  1.$",
